---
import TextPage from '../components/TextPage.astro';

const title = 'About | Playzoni';
const description =
  'Learn about Playzoni, a free browser games site run by SparkBeta Tech in Surat, India, and how we choose and test every game we publish.';
---
<TextPage title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/about" h1="About Playzoni">
  <p>
    Playzoni is a website where you can play free games in your browser. You pick a game, press Play, and it starts. There
    is nothing to download and no account to make. It works on phones, tablets and computers.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Playzoni is run by SparkBeta Tech, a small company based in Surat, India. We are a small team, and we care about making
    a games site that is quick to open, easy to use and honest about what it shows you.
  </p>

  <h2>How we pick games</h2>
  <p>
    We pick games that load quickly, work on phones and computers, and are easy to start. We keep playing and checking
    them, and the games we have tested in depth get a longer page with their controls and our own tips.
  </p>
  <p>
    Every game page has text we wrote ourselves. We do not copy the text that comes with a game, and we do not show
    ratings, play counts or awards unless they are real. If a game stops working or does not work on your device, press
    Report under the game and we will fix it or take it down.
  </p>

  <h2>Where the games come from</h2>
  <p>
    Games on Playzoni come from independent developers and game publishing platforms. Each game stays the work of its
    developer, and we show the developer's name on the game page when we know it.
  </p>

  <h2>Free to play</h2>
  <p>
    Playzoni is free to use. To pay for running the site, we may show ads in the future. If we do, they will not cover the
    game or get in the way of playing it.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact us</h2>
  <p>
    Questions, problems with a game, or ideas for the site? Write to us at
    <a href="mailto:hello@playzoni.com">hello@playzoni.com</a>. Game developers can read how to
    <a href="/developers">send us a game</a>.
  </p>
</TextPage>
